    {
      "id": 7980,
      "name": "Hilgendwarf",
      "username": "Hilgendwarf",
      "avatar_template": "/letter_avatar_proxy/v4/letter/h/59ef9b/{size}.png",
      "created_at": "2013-05-16T14:26:12.000Z",
      "cooked": "<p>Hello everyone,</p><p>&nbsp;</p><p>I was playing a game against Spite the other day, and through a combination of 3 cards (Twist the Ether, Lead from the Front, and Next Evolution) I was able to completely negate all of the damage that Spite dealt to the party. &nbsp;I just wanted to check if that was allowed or if it's something I was doing wrong. &nbsp;I'll explain it in detail.</p><p>&nbsp;</p><p>Through Twist the Ether I was able to decide that Spite only dealt Melee damage.</p><p>&nbsp;</p><p>Through Lead from the Front I was able to let Legacy recieve all damage dealt by Spite.</p><p>&nbsp;</p><p>Through Next Evolution I was able to make Legacy immune to Melee damage every turn, thus removing all damage from the party.</p><p>&nbsp;</p><p>Is that correct? &nbsp;Am I using any of those cards incorrectly, or can Spite just be broken that way?</p>",
      "post_number": 1,
      "post_type": 1,
      "updated_at": "2021-02-07T01:38:23.145Z",
      "reply_count": 0,
      "reply_to_post_number": null,
